A||N||4||Eric_PA||Will a 1995 16x8 TA rim fit on an 84 to 87||||5||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||04-27-2001||06:41 AM||||I have a chance to pick up a set of 16x8 inch rims off of a 1995 Trans am. I was wondering if anyone knows if they would fit. I need four new tires this week and would really like to upgrade to 16 inch wheels. I'm just woried about the offsets. By the way I am planning on using 245-45R16's for the front and 245-50R16's for the rear. That is of course if the wheels fit the car properly. This is for an 86 GT.<P>Thanks,<BR>Eric <p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||04-27-2001||08:14 AM||||The offset is *waaay* wrong. And I'm not sure, but I think the bolt pattern diameter is different as well.<P>The Fiero uses the same type of wheels that are found on front-wheel drive cars, not rear-wheel drive.<P>Sorry 'bout that...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||04-27-2001||09:38 AM||||I didn't think they were close, but my friend who is selling them insists that they fit front wheel drive gm cars. He is going to let me borrow them tonight to find out. I'll have to prove to him or he won't shut up until I do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for the input||||reg||7
Z||000003||fyerstarter||04-27-2001||11:08 AM||||The Fiero has a 5x100 bolt pattern, Camaros and Firebirds have 5x120. You will never even get the wheel on the car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-27-2001||03:51 PM||||TA and most GM heavy stuff 5x114.3,  we are 5x100mm.. NOPE.. go fish..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
